<h1>[AAC] WIA AAC Standard</h1>
<h2>Official Ebook - Complete Guide</h2>

<hr>

<blockquote>
<p><strong>Hongik Ingan (弘益人間)</strong></p>
<p>"Benefit All Humanity"</p>
<p>Communication is a fundamental human right. The WIA AAC Standard ensures that assistive technology works together seamlessly, empowering every individual to express themselves.</p>
</blockquote>

<hr>

<h2>About This Ebook</h2>

<p>This official ebook provides a comprehensive guide to the WIA AAC (Augmentative and Alternative Communication) Standard. It covers the complete specification across all four phases, from signal formats to ecosystem integration.</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="10">
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Version</strong></td>
        <td>1.0.0</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Chapters</strong></td>
        <td>8</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Pages</strong></td>
        <td>~110</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>License</strong></td>
        <td>MIT (Free)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Last Updated</strong></td>
        <td>2025</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<hr>

